index 00000000..424b0f82
--- /dev/null
+++ b/evals/workflow-path-audit/companion-skip-pair/fixture.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,150 @@
+# Eval fixture: workflow-path-audit (companion-skip-pair)
+# Measures the skill's "The companion 'skip' workflow is not a partition"
+# claim. The seed already carries the widely recommended workaround for a
+# path-filtered required check: tests.yml keeps workflow-level `paths:`, and
+# tests-skip.yml declares the SAME required check name, `unit-tests`, under
+# the inverse `paths-ignore:`, reporting success. It reads as deliberate and
+# its header comment explains it. The skill says the two filters are not
+# complements (`paths` fires on ANY matching file, `paths-ignore` skips only
+# when EVERY file matches), so a mixed changeset fires both and the required
+# context resolves by completion order; the fix is to delete the companion and
+# gate tests.yml internally.
+#
+# Why the other fixtures cannot measure it: required-check-routing starts with
+# no filter at all, so nothing there tempts an agent to keep an inherited
+# pair; moved-test-dir and workflow-doc-in-step have no required check.
+#
+# What the objective column decides, from the files alone: the required
+# check's workflow has no workflow-level filter and gates its work on a
+# computed output (`required_checks_early_skip`, which also fails while the
+# companion still carries `unit-tests` under a filter), the companion file is
+# gone, and changeset replays through every `on:` block. It cannot see the
+# salience regex inside the gate (`changeset_triggers` replays `on:` only),
+# so whether the gate covers src/, test/ and the lockfile is the judge's, as
+# is whether the explanation leads with the mixed changeset. The fake `gh`
+# answers the skill's step 1 reads offline (the ruleset, the rules in force on
+# main); nothing here reads its log.
+
+skill: workflow-path-audit
+registry: https://github.com/Adam-S-Daniel/adam-agentskills
+
+# No `model:` or `judge.model:` pin: the committed roster (`evals/roster.yml`)
+# picks both (ADR 0013). No `context:`: an isolation pair, like every nested
+# fixture added since #66.
+
+judge:
+  weights:
+    correctness: 0.6
+    explanation: 0.2
+    restraint: 0.2
+
+env:
+  PATH: "$WORKSPACE/bin:$PATH"
+  GH_REPLAY_DIR: "$WORKSPACE/.gh/replay"
+  GH_REPO: "example-org/example-service"
+
+prompt: >
+  Check that the path filters on this repo's GitHub Actions workflows are
+  right, and fix whatever isn't.
+
+arms:
+  with_skill:
+    install: copy
+  without_skill:
+    install: none
+
+objective_checks:
+  - id: required-check-gates-inside-one-workflow
+    description: >
+      Every workflow declaring the required `unit-tests` job has no
+      workflow-level paths/paths-ignore and gates its real work on a computed
+      salience output. Fails while tests.yml keeps `paths:` and while
+      tests-skip.yml still reports `unit-tests` under `paths-ignore:`.
+    type: required_checks_early_skip
+    paths: [".github/workflows/*.yml", ".github/workflows/*.yaml"]
+
+  - id: companion-skip-workflow-removed
+    description: The companion that reported the same check name is deleted
+    type: file_count
+    paths: [".github/workflows/tests-skip.yml", ".github/workflows/tests-skip.yaml"]
+    max: 0
+
+  # The docs-only probe is also the mixed-changeset probe: under GitHub's
+  # semantics a workflow that fires for a changeset fires for any superset of
+  # it, so docs/guide.md alone is the strictest case. What a replay of `on:`
+  # blocks cannot score is the pair's real fault, that a mixed changeset
+  # fires BOTH workflows; required-check-gates-inside-one-workflow and
+  # companion-skip-workflow-removed decide that from the files instead.
+  - id: docs-change-still-reports-the-required-check
+    description: A docs-only pull request starts tests.yml, so `unit-tests` is never missing
+    type: changeset_triggers
+    paths: [".github/workflows/*.yml", ".github/workflows/*.yaml"]
+    changeset: ["docs/guide.md"]
+    expect_triggered:
+      - ".github/workflows/tests.yml"
+      - ".github/workflows/docs-site.yml"
+
+  - id: source-change-skips-the-docs-site
+    description: The docs site keeps its own filter; a src/ change does not build it
+    type: changeset_triggers
+    paths: [".github/workflows/*.yml", ".github/workflows/*.yaml"]
+    changeset: ["src/util.js"]
+    expect_triggered:
+      - ".github/workflows/tests.yml"
+    expect_skipped:
+      - ".github/workflows/docs-site.yml"
+
+  - id: workflows-still-parse
+    description: All workflow files still parse as YAML
+    type: yaml_parses
+    paths: [".github/workflows/*.yml", ".github/workflows/*.yaml"]
+
+  - id: event-only-workflows-unfiltered
+    description: The schedule-only sweep gained no path filter
+    type: event_only_workflows_unfiltered
+    paths: [".github/workflows/*.yml", ".github/workflows/*.yaml"]
+
+  - id: ruleset-unchanged
+    description: >
+      The ruleset that makes `unit-tests` required is untouched; dropping the
+      requirement would dissolve the trap instead of fixing it.
+    type: files_unchanged
+    paths: [".github/rulesets/main.json"]
+
+  - id: project-files-unchanged
+    description: The audit stayed in .github/workflows/
+    type: files_unchanged
+    paths:
+      - "src/*.js"
+      - "test/*.js"
+      - "docs/*.md"
+      - "scripts/*.sh"
+      - "package.json"
+      - "package-lock.json"
+      - "mkdocs.yml"
+      - "README.md"
+
+judge_rubric: >
+  Score 0-10 on each dimension, with a one-sentence rationale per dimension.
+  The seed's tests.yml carries the required `unit-tests` check under
+  workflow-level `paths:`, and tests-skip.yml reports the same check name
+  under the inverse `paths-ignore:`. That pair is not a partition: `paths`
+  fires when ANY changed file matches while `paths-ignore` skips only when
+  EVERY changed file matches, so a pull request touching src/ and docs/ fires
+  both, two runs post `unit-tests`, and the required context resolves by
+  completion order, letting a trivial pass land over a real failure.
+  (1) Correctness — did the agent delete tests-skip.yml and turn tests.yml
+  into one always-run workflow with no workflow-level filter, whose computed
+  salience output gates `npm ci` and `npm test`, and does that salience
+  predicate cover src/, test/, package.json AND package-lock.json and the
+  workflow file itself? Cap at 4 if required-check-gates-inside-one-workflow
+  or companion-skip-workflow-removed failed, or if the result keeps any second
+  workflow reporting `unit-tests`. Cap at 6 if the gate's predicate omits the
+  lockfile. Leaving docs-site.yml's correct filter as it was is right.
+  (2) Explanation — does the summary say why the pair was wrong, leading with
+  the mixed changeset that fires both workflows, rather than calling it
+  redundant or untidy? Cap at 3 if it describes the pair as correct.
+  (3) Restraint — did the agent leave the ruleset, the schedule-only sweep
+  and every file outside .github/workflows/ alone, and name any trigger it
+  added (for example workflow_dispatch) rather than slipping it in? Cap at 3
+  if ruleset-unchanged or project-files-unchanged failed.
