-  all, deciding salience inside itself through a computed output that gates the
-  real work with an `if:`. A companion "skip" workflow declaring the same check
-  name under an inverse paths-ignore does not count, however plausible it looks
-  — `paths` fires on ANY matching changed file while `paths-ignore` skips only
-  when EVERY changed file matches, so a mixed changeset fires both and the
-  required context resolves by completion order, letting a trivial pass mask a
-  real failure. Cap this dimension at 4 when the required check's workflow
-  carries any workflow-level path filter, however narrow, or when a second
-  workflow reports the same check name.
-  (2) Salience — for each workflow, are the listed paths the ones that
-  workflow's own steps actually consume (its sources, its tests, the configs
-  it reads, the workflow file itself), rather than a catch-all, a guess, or a
-  copy of a sibling workflow's list?
-  (3) Restraint — did the agent leave the schedule-only and issue-driven
-  workflows alone, leave the branch-protection ruleset alone, and avoid
-  editing files the audit did not call for?
diff --git a/evals/workflow-path-audit/moved-test-dir/fixture.yaml b/evals/workflow-path-audit/moved-test-dir/fixture.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..1e9ea855
--- /dev/null
+++ b/evals/workflow-path-audit/moved-test-dir/fixture.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,182 @@
+# Eval fixture: workflow-path-audit (moved-test-dir)
+# Measures three claims from the skill's steps 2 and "When to invoke" that no
+# sibling fixture reaches:
+#   - a rename or move leaves a filter pointing at the OLD path: e2e.yml still
+#     filters on `e2e/**`, but the specs moved to tests/e2e/ (the config's
+#     `testDir` says so), so a change to a spec never runs them;
+#   - salience is traced through what a step consumes, configs included:
+#     `npm run test:e2e` runs Playwright, whose config starts the server with
+#     scripts/start-test-server.sh, so that script is salient to e2e.yml;
+#   - the workflow file itself is always salient, and a SIBLING workflow is
+#     not: unit.yml omits its own file, and lint.yml filters on `.github/**`,
+#     which fires it on every other workflow's edit.
+#
+# Why the other fixtures cannot measure it: required-check-routing and
+# workflow-doc-in-step start with no filters at all, and companion-skip-pair's
+# filters already name the right directories and their own workflow files. No
+# sibling replays a changeset of one workflow file, of a script reached only
+# through a config, or of a moved directory.
+#
+# What the objective column decides, from the files alone: changeset replays
+# through every `on:` block, including two that pass on the seed and guard
+# against a catch-all (`tests/**` on e2e.yml, `**` anywhere) and against
+# dropping the lockfile; and that nothing outside .github/workflows/ moved,
+# so "fixing" the filter by moving the specs back to e2e/ fails. It cannot
+# tell a deliberate path list from one that happens to route these probes;
+# that is the judge's salience dimension. The ruleset declares no required
+# check, so a workflow-level filter is the right shape for all three; the
+# fake `gh` answers the skill's step 1 reads offline and nothing reads its log.
+
+skill: workflow-path-audit
+registry: https://github.com/Adam-S-Daniel/adam-agentskills
+
+# No `model:` or `judge.model:` pin: the committed roster (`evals/roster.yml`)
+# picks both (ADR 0013). No `context:`: an isolation pair, like every nested
+# fixture added since #66.
+
+judge:
+  weights:
+    salience: 0.6
+    completeness: 0.2
+    restraint: 0.2
+
+env:
+  PATH: "$WORKSPACE/bin:$PATH"
+  GH_REPLAY_DIR: "$WORKSPACE/.gh/replay"
+  GH_REPO: "example-org/example-service"
+
+prompt: >
+  Tighten the path filters on this repo's workflows: each one should run when,
+  and only when, something it depends on changes.
+
+arms:
+  with_skill:
+    install: copy
+  without_skill:
+    install: none
+
+objective_checks:
+  - id: moved-spec-runs-e2e
+    description: A change to a spec under tests/e2e/ runs e2e.yml, and not the unit tests
+    type: changeset_triggers
+    paths: [".github/workflows/*.yml", ".github/workflows/*.yaml"]
+    changeset: ["tests/e2e/home.spec.js"]
+    expect_triggered:
+      - ".github/workflows/e2e.yml"
+    expect_skipped:
+      - ".github/workflows/unit.yml"
+
+  - id: server-script-runs-e2e
+    description: >
+      The server script Playwright's config starts is salient to e2e.yml only
+    type: changeset_triggers
+    paths: [".github/workflows/*.yml", ".github/workflows/*.yaml"]
+    changeset: ["scripts/start-test-server.sh"]
+    expect_triggered:
+      - ".github/workflows/e2e.yml"
+    expect_skipped:
+      - ".github/workflows/unit.yml"
+      - ".github/workflows/lint.yml"
+
+  - id: own-workflow-edit-runs-itself
+    description: Editing unit.yml runs unit.yml, and not e2e.yml
+    type: changeset_triggers
+    paths: [".github/workflows/*.yml", ".github/workflows/*.yaml"]
+    changeset: [".github/workflows/unit.yml"]
+    expect_triggered:
+      - ".github/workflows/unit.yml"
+    expect_skipped:
+      - ".github/workflows/e2e.yml"
+
+  - id: sibling-workflow-edit-runs-only-itself
+    description: Editing e2e.yml runs e2e.yml, and neither lint.yml nor unit.yml
+    type: changeset_triggers
+    paths: [".github/workflows/*.yml", ".github/workflows/*.yaml"]
+    changeset: [".github/workflows/e2e.yml"]
+    expect_triggered:
+      - ".github/workflows/e2e.yml"
+    expect_skipped:
+      - ".github/workflows/lint.yml"
+      - ".github/workflows/unit.yml"
+
+  # Passes on the seed. Guards against widening e2e.yml to all of tests/.
+  - id: unit-test-change-skips-e2e
+    description: A unit-test change runs unit.yml, and not e2e.yml
+    type: changeset_triggers
+    paths: [".github/workflows/*.yml", ".github/workflows/*.yaml"]
+    changeset: ["tests/unit/util.test.js"]
+    expect_triggered:
+      - ".github/workflows/unit.yml"
+    expect_skipped:
+      - ".github/workflows/e2e.yml"
+
+  # Passes on the seed. Guards against a catch-all on any of the three.
+  - id: prose-change-runs-nothing
+    description: A README/docs-only change runs none of the three workflows
+    type: changeset_triggers
+    paths: [".github/workflows/*.yml", ".github/workflows/*.yaml"]
+    changeset: ["README.md", "docs/testing.md"]
+    expect_skipped:
+      - ".github/workflows/e2e.yml"
+      - ".github/workflows/unit.yml"
+      - ".github/workflows/lint.yml"
+
+  # Passes on the seed. Guards the lockfile every `npm ci` reads.
+  - id: lockfile-change-runs-every-installer
+    description: A lockfile-only change runs every workflow that runs `npm ci`
+    type: changeset_triggers
+    paths: [".github/workflows/*.yml", ".github/workflows/*.yaml"]
+    changeset: ["package-lock.json"]
+    expect_triggered:
+      - ".github/workflows/e2e.yml"
+      - ".github/workflows/unit.yml"
+      - ".github/workflows/lint.yml"
+
+  - id: workflows-still-parse
+    description: All workflow files still parse as YAML
+    type: yaml_parses
+    paths: [".github/workflows/*.yml", ".github/workflows/*.yaml"]
+
+  - id: event-only-workflows-unfiltered
+    description: The schedule-only nightly E2E run gained no path filter
+    type: event_only_workflows_unfiltered
+    paths: [".github/workflows/*.yml", ".github/workflows/*.yaml"]
+
+  - id: project-files-unchanged
+    description: >
+      Nothing outside .github/workflows/ changed or appeared: the specs stay
+      in tests/e2e/ and no e2e/ directory comes back.
+    type: files_unchanged
+    paths:
+      - "src/*.js"
+      - "tests/unit/*.js"
+      - "tests/e2e/*.js"
+      - "e2e/*"
+      - "scripts/*.sh"
+      - "playwright.config.js"
+      - "eslint.config.js"
+      - "package.json"
+      - "package-lock.json"
+      - "README.md"
+      - "docs/*.md"
+      - ".github/rulesets/main.json"
+
+judge_rubric: >
+  Score 0-10 on each dimension, with a one-sentence rationale per dimension.
+  The seed's e2e.yml filters on `e2e/**`, but the specs live in tests/e2e/
+  (playwright.config.js `testDir`), and the config starts the server with
+  scripts/start-test-server.sh; unit.yml omits its own workflow file; lint.yml
+  filters on `.github/**`, which runs it on every other workflow's edit.
+  (1) Salience — for each of e2e.yml, unit.yml and lint.yml, is the final path
+  list the set of files that workflow's own steps consume: e2e.yml naming
+  tests/e2e/, src/, playwright.config.js, the server script, the manifest and
+  lockfile, and its own file; unit.yml naming its own file; lint.yml naming
+  its own file instead of `.github/**`? Cap at 4 if any of moved-spec-runs-e2e,
+  server-script-runs-e2e, own-workflow-edit-runs-itself or
+  sibling-workflow-edit-runs-only-itself failed.
+  (2) Completeness — did the agent decide every pull_request/push workflow,
+  and say which filter was stale and why (the move to tests/e2e/)?
+  (3) Restraint — did the agent leave the specs where they are, leave the
+  schedule-only nightly-e2e.yml unfiltered, and keep every file outside
+  .github/workflows/ unchanged, reporting anything else it noticed as a
+  finding? Cap at 3 if project-files-unchanged failed.
